 Add `--json` to get a JSON object instead.
 
+### Caching
+
+Parsing dominates the runtime on large files. Pass `--cache` to store the
+parsed records on disk and reuse them on the next run over the same file:
+
+```
+logslice --cache huge.log --count-by level   # parses and caches
+logslice --cache huge.log --level error      # served from the cache
+```
+
+Cached results are stored as JSON, one entry per log file. The cache
+directory is resolved at run time: `$LOGSLICE_CACHE_DIR` if set, else
+`$XDG_CACHE_HOME/logslice`, else `~/.cache/logslice`.
+
+The cache key includes the file's resolved path, size and modification time,
+so editing or appending to a log invalidates its entry. Entries also expire
+after a TTL (`--cache-ttl SECONDS`, default 3600); an expired entry is
+re-parsed and overwritten on the next `--cache` run. Delete the cache
+directory to clear it.
+
 ## Development
 
 ```
